    rule1Title: "1. FDA 21 CFR § 179.41 Cumulative Radiant Fluence Ceiling (≤ 12.0 J/cm²)",
    rule1Text: "Federal regulations strictly dictate that pulsed light treatment of commercial food items shall not exceed an integrated cumulative radiant fluence of 12.0 J/cm². Treatment must utilize xenon flashlamps emitting broad-spectrum radiation (200 to 1100 nm) with pulse durations not exceeding 2.0 milliseconds. Exceeding 12.0 J/cm² causes excessive surface lipid peroxidation, sensory off-flavors in dairy and egg matrices, and regulatory non-compliance.",
