    rule2Text: "Xenon lamps convert up to 60-70% of electrical energy into intense conductive and radiant heat. Without active forced vortex air or chilled jacket cooling, quartz sleeve surface temperatures reach 260°C to 340°C. If cold washdown water (10°C-25°C) from sanitation sprays or HVAC condensation drips onto unshielded hot quartz, thermal contraction shock (ΔT > 140°C) shatters the silica tube, contaminating food conveyors with sharp glass debris. Sleeves must maintain NSF/3-A food-safe containment guards.",
