    rule3Text: "Xenon arc radiation below 240 nm photolyzes ambient atmospheric oxygen (O2 + hν → 2O; O + O2 → O3), producing highly toxic ozone gas. Industrial HIPL conveyor enclosures generate 15 to 45 ppm of ozone in the flash zone. High-capacity exhaust blowers must route air through heated manganese dioxide/copper oxide (MnO2/CuO) catalytic destruct units with ≥ 99.5% conversion efficiency to guarantee discharge air remains well below the OSHA PEL (0.1 ppm 8-hr TWA, 0.3 ppm STEL).",
    rule4Title: "4. Class 3B/4 Optical Flash Radiation Shielding & High-Voltage Interlocks",
    rule4Text: "Microsecond xenon flash lamps emit megawatt pulses of ultraviolet and intense visible light capable of causing immediate photokeratitis (welder's flash), corneal erythema, and retinal burns. All conveyor infeed and discharge apertures must incorporate serpentine labyrinth light traps providing minimum Optical Density (OD) ≥ 8. Access panels must be fitted with dual-channel category 4 safety switches that automatically dump high-voltage capacitor charges (≤ 50 V within 2.0 s per NFPA 79).",
